{
 "_doc": [
  "Shared money wire-format vectors (build contract section 1, as amended by ADR 0003 section 1a).",
  "Every language's test suite loads this file: detection-py (tests/test_money_vectors.py),",
  "orchestrator-go (internal/client/money_vectors_test.go), apps/dashboard-ts (tests/money.test.ts).",
  "ledger-rust does not load it yet: 'ledger_append_expected' is the verdict POST /ledger/append",
  "should give for amount_usd (a positive-only field) once the ledger adopts the amended bound.",
  "As of Sep 24 2026 the ledger still accepts over-bound canonical strings (e.g. '1000000000000000.00').",
  "'money' = a field that allows 0.00; 'positive_money' = a positive-only field.",
  "string_vectors: 'input' is the JSON string value. json_vectors: 'json' is the raw JSON text of the value;",
  "the verdict applies to a positive-only money field (e.g. LabeledValue.amount_usd)."
 ],
 "contract": {
  "pattern": "^(0|[1-9][0-9]{0,14})\\.[0-9]{2}$",
  "max": "999999999999999.99",
  "max_integer_digits": 15,
  "max_length": 18
 },
